"page_start": "347", "journal_title": "NOONE"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "82", "artid": "309", "page_start": "309", "journal_title": "NOONE"}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "54", "artid": "5042", "page_start": "5042", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "130", "artid": "2529", "page_start": "2529", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9152"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "131", "artid": "2766", "page_start": "2766", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}}, "curated_relation": false, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/9024"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "50", "artid": "5122", "page_start": "5122", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev."}}}], "number_of_pages": 4, "referenced_authors_bais": ["R.J.Glauber.1", "P.Kwiat.1", "T.J.Herzog.1", "H.Weinfurter.1", "A.Zeilinger.1"], "figures": [{"filename": "figure1.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "A proposed quantum eraser experiment. A pair of entangled photons is emitted from either atom A or atom B by atomic cascade decay. ``Clicks\" at $D_{3}$ or $D_{4}$ provide which-path information and ``clicks\" at $D_{1}$ or $D_{2}$ erase the which-path information.", "label": "fig:figure1", "source": "arxiv", "key": "0f5dc3d30c92bcda4ed3fe0127717ca1", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/0f5dc3d30c92bcda4ed3fe0127717ca1"}, {"filename": "figure2.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Schematic of the experimental setup. The pump laser beam of SPDC is divided by a double-slit and incident onto a BBO crystal at two regions A and B. A pair of signal-idler photons is generated either from A or B region. The detection time of the signal photon is $8ns$ earlier than that of the idler.", "label": "fig:figure2", "source": "arxiv", "key": "e632cffbb738c7abb04afb2227dc5037", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/e632cffbb738c7abb04afb2227dc5037"}, {"filename": "figure3.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "$R_{01}$ (``joint detection'' rate between detectors $D_{0}$ and $ D_{1}$) against the $x$ coordinates of detector $D_{0}$. A standard Young's double-slit interference pattern is observed.", "label": "fig:figure3", "source": "arxiv", "key": "300f7481ae2d67c566049a5d2704fab1", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/300f7481ae2d67c566049a5d2704fab1"}, {"filename": "figure4.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "$R_{02}$ (``joint detection'' rate between detectors $D_{0}$ and $ D_{2}$) Note, there is a $\\pi$ phase shift compare to $R_{01}$ shown in Fig.\\ref{fig:figure3}", "label": "fig:figure4", "source": "arxiv", "key": "93f02ee1f41cfcd0f1edb69901893bc6", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/93f02ee1f41cfcd0f1edb69901893bc6"}, {"filename": "figure5.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "$R_{03}$ (``joint detection'' rate between detectors $D_{0}$ and $ D_{3}$). An absence of interference is clearly demonstrated.", "label": "fig:figure5", "source": "arxiv", "key": "c52cde5efd71d15cb960e1abc1c79757", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/c52cde5efd71d15cb960e1abc1c79757"}], "legacy_version": "20160616173442.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "1999-03-16", "preprint_date": "1999-03", "author_count": 5, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "twocolumn, 4pages, submitted to PRL"}], "first_author": {"full_name": "Kim, Yoon-Ho", "last_name": "Kim", "first_name": "Yoon-Ho", "recid": 1947828}, "control_number": 496803, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.84.1"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.84.1"}], "earliest_date": "1999-03", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Kim:1999rj"], "abstracts": [{"value": "This paper reports a \"delayed choice quantum eraser\" experiment proposed by Scully and Dr\\\"{u}hl in 1982. The experimental results demonstrated the possibility of simultaneously observing both particle-like and wave-like behavior of a quantum via quantum entanglement. The which-path or both-path information of a quantum can be erased or marked by its entangled twin even after the registration of the quantum."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "This paper reports a \"delayed choice quantum eraser\" experiment proposed by Scully and Drühl in 1982. The experimental results demonstrated the possibility of simultaneously observing both particle-like and wave-like behavior of a quantum via quantum entanglement. The which-path or both-path information of a quantum can be erased or marked by its entangled twin even after the registration of the quantum.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "2000PhRvL..84....1K"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-3995380"}], "titles": [{"title": "A delayed choice quantum eraser"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "A Delayed Choice Quantum Eraser"}], "facet_author_name": ["1906428_M.O. Scully", "1951066_Sergei P. Kulik", "1947828_Y.H. Kim", "2040268_Rui Yu", "2458450_Hsin-Yi Shih"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:496803", "updated": "2025-10-01T09:53:18.403745"}, "curated": false, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys. Rev. Lett.", "Phys.Rev.Lett."], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/9903047"}]}, "created": "1999-03-16T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2025-10-01T09:53:18.403745+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/496803?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/496803?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/496803?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/496803?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/496803?format=json-exp